{
  "_comment": "Bay5 ArenaMode integration, 2026-09-21. Coordinates derived from Arena source AI bearing points and checked in the native map. Four Player/All points distribute respawns across both ends; bot markers are separate. Background port moves the northeast-lane bot 3 m south to avoid automatic placement on a disconnected container-side patch; see docs/progress/bay5-background.md. No loot or Scav raids. 2026-10-25 (docs/progress/door-poses.md): player-north-west moved (54.2, 53.8) -> (55.2, 53.0) and the east-lane bot (117.8917, 43.099) -> (118.3, 44.4) because both stood on the edge of the NavMesh (0.03 m and 0.09 m of clearance, outside the mesh); the new points have 1.25 m and 1.28 m of clearance in the play component. 2026-11-12 (spawn rows, user request; rules R1/R2/R5 of the spawn-count work): six Bot rows are APPENDED after the ten originals, which stay byte-identical (ArenaMode pins bot-west-centre by id and exact floats). Why more rows: ArenaMode's burst selector uses only Bot rows at least 25 m (3D) from the player, and Tactical needs five of them from wherever the leader stands. Four rows stand on Arena's own AI core points of LastHero_AI (core-08 = AICore ID:8, core-07 = ID:7, core-03 = ID:3, core-06 = ID:6), two are mesh fill points (fill-01 at (80, 24), fill-02 at (64, 58), no native marker passes there); every row lies on the play component of the built NavMesh, at least 12 m from the capture-point light, at least 15 m from every parked gate part (pinned). fill-02 is the tightest row: 10.1 m from player-north-west and from the nearest other row, so a host nudge of either row by 0.2 m would break the 10 m floors of the tests. Offline coverage (tools/validate/spawn_coverage.py): the original ten rows already gave every NavMesh cell outside the pockets at least five rows farther than 25 m (minimum 6, median 8); with the six new rows the minimum is 9, the median 12 and the mean distance to the nearest row falls from 12.2 m to 9.1 m. The rows add variety, not coverage. Offline, host check pending.",
